{%- comment -%}
  ═══ LBASS — SALE PERCENTAGE ═══

  Echoes the discount percentage as a bare integer, or `0` when the piece is not
  genuinely marked down. Nothing else. No markup, no whitespace.

  ── WHY THIS IS ITS OWN FILE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Three surfaces print a percentage for the same product: the badge on the card
  image, the pill in the card price row, and the product page. If each does its
  own arithmetic they can disagree, and a shopper who sees «‑35%» on the grid
  and «‑36%» on the product page has been shown two different claims about one
  price. templates/product.liquid did exactly that until 2026-09-10: it used a
  plain `divided_by`, which FLOORS on integers, while snippets/lbass-price
  rounded half-up. On a 300 -> 193 markdown that is 35% against 36%.

  The subtraction (`compare_at - price`) is not here on purpose. It is exact,
  has no rounding behaviour to get wrong, and callers that need the money value
  do it inline. Only the part that can drift is centralised.

  ── ROUNDING ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Liquid's `divided_by` floors on integers, so a naive percentage reads low:
  31.7% prints as 31. Going through per-mille and adding 5 before the final
  divide rounds half-up instead, so the number matches what a shopper gets
  dividing the two printed prices themselves.

  ── ELIGIBILITY ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  A percentage exists if and ONLY if Shopify's own `variant.compare_at_price` is
  set and is greater than the price being charged — a former price the shop
  actually asked for. The running campaign does not qualify (it discounts the
  SECOND item, not this one) and neither does `lbass.retail_ref` (what the model
  costs new, which was never our price). See snippets/lbass-price.liquid.

  ── PARAMETERS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    product   required
    variant   optional — defaults to selected_or_first_available_variant

  USAGE
      {%- capture pct %}{% render 'lbass-sale', product: product %}{% endcapture -%}
      {%- assign pct = pct | strip -%}
      {%- if pct != '0' -%} ... {%- endif -%}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign lbs_v = variant | default: product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  assign lbs_price = lbs_v.price | default: product.price
  assign lbs_cap = lbs_v.compare_at_price

  assign lbs_pct = 0
  if lbs_cap and lbs_cap > lbs_price
    assign lbs_save = lbs_cap | minus: lbs_price
    assign lbs_pct = lbs_save | times: 1000 | divided_by: lbs_cap | plus: 5 | divided_by: 10
  endif
  echo lbs_pct
-%}
